{
  "hypothesis": "Improve memory locality and loop order by using a blocked approach to process submatrices in larger chunks without resetting the sum incorrectly.",
  "transformations": [
    "Reorganize loops to improve cache performance by processing blocks of data together.",
    "Use blocking to reduce cache misses by keeping submatrices in cache for longer."
  ],
  "sources_kept": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "src/solution.cpp",
      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <climits>\n\nint main() {\n\tint n, s;\n\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\n\tstd::vector<std::vector<int>> matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; j++) \n\t\t\tscanf(\"%d\", &(matrix[i][j]));\n\n\tassert(s < n);\n\tassert(n < 8000);\n\tassert(s > 0);\n\tassert(n > 0);\n\n\tconst int blockSize = 32; // Define a block size for blocking\n\tint mxSum = INT_MIN;\n\n\tfor (int bi = 0; bi < n; bi += blockSize) {\n\t\tfor (int bj = 0; bj < n; bj += blockSize) {\n\t\t\tint sum = 0;\n\t\t\t// Initialize the first block\n\t\t\tfor (int i = bi; i < std::min(bi + blockSize, n); i++) {\n\t\t\t\tfor (int j = bj; j < std::min(bj + blockSize, n); j++) {\n\t\t\t\t\tif (i < s && j < s) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tsum += matrix[i][j];\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\n\n\t\t\t// Slide the block horizontally and vertically\n\t\t\tfor (int iOffset = 0; iOffset <= n - s; iOffset++) {\n\t\t\t\tif (iOffset > 0) {\n\t\t\t\t\t// Move the block down by one row\n\t\t\t\t\tint exitingRow = bi + std::min(blockSize, n - bi) - 1;\n\t\t\t\t\tint enteringRow = exitingRow + 1;\n\t\t\t\t\tif (enteringRow < n) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tfor (int j = bj; j < std::min(bj + blockSize, n); j++) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsum -= matrix[exitingRow][j];\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif (enteringRow < s) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsum += matrix[enteringRow][j];\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tfor (int jOffset = 0; jOffset <= n - s; jOffset++) {\n\t\t\t\tif (jOffset > 0) {\n\t\t\t\t\t// Move the block right by one column\n\t\t\t\t\tint exitingCol = bj + std::min(blockSize, n - bj) - 1;\n\t\t\t\t\tint enteringCol = exitingCol + 1;\n\t\t\t\t\tif (enteringCol < n) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tfor (int i = bi; i < std::min(bi + blockSize, n); i++) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsum -= matrix[i][exitingCol];\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif (enteringCol < s) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsum += matrix[i][enteringCol];\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tprintf(\"%d\\n\", mxSum);\n}"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "This experiment introduces a blocking approach to improve memory locality and loop order. The matrix is divided into blocks of size 'blockSize', and the algorithm processes these blocks to find the maximum sum submatrix."
}
